As far as I know there are no 'AI generated' conlangs, at least not any that are any good.
If you look at AULE, you'll see it is not a good language for humans to use.

There is still a live long chat copy bug with chatGPT web interface.
Generating AULE from the ELED alphabet was a fast way to produce long test data that reliably produces error conditions.
It as also a quick way to test the chat copy but on a different browser while logged out.

If anybody tries to present AULE as an example of why chatbots should not create conlangs, they are correct.
If anybody tries to present AULE as an example of a conlang generated by a chatbot, they may be misled, or misleading.
